        "name": "correctness",
        "score": 9,
        "rationale": "Removes the on.pull_request.paths filter, so the workflow and the required `test` check run on every PR. It checks out with fetch-depth: 0, so origin/<base_ref> is available for the diff. The early `Detect site changes` step (id: changes) writes site=true/false to GITHUB_OUTPUT based on a three-dot diff filtered by '^site/'. The later build/test step is gated with `if: steps.changes.outputs.site == 'true'`, so a docs-only PR skips it and the job ends success. Leaving `pull_request:` with a null value is valid YAML and triggers on the default PR activity types. Minor gaps: only one later step is gated, though that is all the workflow has, and the change is unverified. The agent stated plainly that it had not run it."
      },
